  "slug": "review-customer-dues-after-sync",
  "title": "Checking a Recent Receipt Before Following Up on a Customer Balance",
  "description": "Verify a receipt or credit note in the ledger before asking a customer to pay an older outstanding amount.",
  "category": "Stock and balances",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Start with the most recent payment evidence",
      "body": "If the customer says they paid, record the amount, date and reference they provided. Look for a related receipt in the correct party ledger. A similar amount alone is not enough to identify the payment."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Compare the source and the synced ledger",
      "body": "In TallyPrime, check the recorded voucher date, type and number. Compare those with the same ledger in Syncora. If the source entry is newer than the last successful sync, wait for a fresh comparison before using the dashboard balance."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Confirm the balance before contacting the customer",
      "body": "Ask the accounting team to reconcile any unmatched receipt or credit note. Check for a difference between the selected period and the balance you plan to quote. When you follow up, use an as-of date and the confirmed amount."
    }
  ],
